  "body": "The group server should be a completely independent server from the homeserver or any other component in a matrix system. Having this separation allows for third party group servers and enhanced functionality, above and beyond what synapse may provide. \r\n\r\nThe current situation is that group information comes down /sync, which effectively prevents the group server from being ripped away from synapse. The third party server could do some mitm handling of /sync, however that feels silly.\r\n\r\nFurther, the group server should get it's own series of endpoints (like the media repo). Instead of being under the client namespace, it should be under the `groups` namespace or similar (`/_matrix/groups/r0/whatever`).\r\n\r\nI've filed this issue here for visibility, and the lack of spec. It would be greatly appreciated if the group server can be handled outside of synapse.\r\n",
